title: "Seasonal attention and spatial evaluation design for Landsat-based ranking of mapped fault-trace proxies: code, frozen protocols, aggregated results and public data"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/haoqi222/seasonal-attention-fault-trace-proxy"
url: "https://github.com/haoqi222/seasonal-attention-fault-trace-proxy"
keywords:
  - geospatial machine learning
  - spatial cross-validation
  - data leakage
  - seasonal attention
  - Landsat
  - fault trace proxy
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocols, aggregated results and a public-data package for the
  study of how evaluation design and spatial position determine apparent
  performance when Landsat-based deep models rank pixels by proximity to mapped
  fault traces. A matched random-pixel holdout yields average precision above
  0.999 for every model, whereas four geographically blocked folds place all
  models at or below the prevalence reference in the southernmost fold.
